xmodel/sol-h5a.md:120:The right member is exactly \(D_{h,F}\) under the Q-value. The coarse value would instead be \(L_0d_{h,F}\), which is not integral in general. The \(x\)-chart argument is symmetric. Statement 3.8 says \(D_{h,F}\in\mathbb Z\) for *every* polynomial \(h\) and every vertex. Thus the Q-value is uniformly compatible with that statement, while the explicit witness in Section 3 refutes a uniform P-value convention. [SIGRAY-AUDIT.md:37](../SIGRAY-AUDIT.md#L37) records the conclusion and an independent nonintegral witness; [SIGRAY-AUDIT.md:92](../SIGRAY-AUDIT.md#L92) records its load-bearing consequence.
